* Simple tracked behavioral op-amp macromodel for GBW-sensitivity studies.
* Pin order matches OPAx320.lib for drop-in substitution: IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT
* Model: single differential input with input capacitance CIN (split IN+/IN-
* to ground, approximating the vendor part's common-mode input caps), a
* two-pole open-loop gain block (dominant pole set by GBW/A0, a non-dominant
* pole at P2MULT*GBW to give a finite/realistic phase margin at crossover),
* and a linear output (AC small-signal use only; no rail clamp). No noise, no CMRR/
* PSRR, no slew-rate limiting, no output impedance -- intentionally minimal,
* used only to sweep GBW (10/20/30 MHz) for closed-loop stability trends and
* cross-checked against the vendor model at 20 MHz. Document as a modeling
* limitation in the report.
.SUBCKT OPAMP_BEH INP INM VCC VEE OUT PARAMS: GBW=20MEG A0=100K P2MULT=4 CIN=9P
* Input capacitance to ground (AC-equivalent to the vendor model's 9 pF total
* input capacitance already assumed elsewhere in the testbenches).
Cinp INP 0 {CIN/2}
Cinm INM 0 {CIN/2}
* Two-pole open-loop voltage gain block, Laplace transfer from (INP-INM) to
* an internal unclamped output node.
Eol OL 0 INP INM Laplace=A0/((1+s/(2*pi*(GBW/A0)))*(1+s/(2*pi*(P2MULT*GBW))))
Rol OL 0 1
* Linear unity output buffer. No rail clamp: an IF()-based clamp prevented
* LTspice .op convergence, and this model is used for small-signal AC GBW
* sensitivity only. Saturation behavior comes from the vendor model.
Eout OUT 0 OL 0 1
.ENDS OPAMP_BEH
